; Thesis figure 15: square calls the * operator, itself a hyperfunction with unlimited versions.
; The two arguments of the call are the same variable, so the entry contexts of * keep a and b
; in one equivalence class (a/b) and a single type test covers both.
function square(x)
A:  call *(x, x) -> B
B:  return #res

function * (a, b) limit=none
T:  if fixnum?(a) goto U else goto X
U:  tmp = fx*?(a, b)
    if tmp goto V else goto W
V:  return tmp
W:  return ##*(a, b)
X:  if flonum?(a) goto Z else goto Y
Y:  return ##*(a, b)
Z:  return fl*(a, b)
